---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import Playground from '../islands/Playground.vue'
---
<Layout
  title="Playground — Parsanol"
  description="Edit an input and watch the parsanol wasm engine build the tree, live in your browser."
  active="playground"
>
  <div class="prose max-w-none mb-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">Grammar playground</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
      Pick a compiled PARG artifact, edit the input, and watch the wasm engine parse it live.
      Every tree is produced by the same <code>@parsanol/wasm</code> binary that the Rust and
      Ruby conformance suites validate, and the badge reports the artifact's embedded tests
      replayed on that binary.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Playground client:only="vue" />

  <section class="prose max-w-none mt-12 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">What runs where</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Artifacts are checksummed <code>parsanol-tree/v2</code> envelopes compiled ahead of
        time; the browser verifies the checksum before parsing.
      </li>
      <li>
        Parsing, bindings application, and the embedded self-test all run in the wasm engine
        (~1.4&nbsp;MB, <code>@parsanol/wasm</code> 0.18.10). No network calls, no server-side
        parsing.
      </li>
      <li>
        A failed parse returns the engine's recovery envelope: byte offset, line/column, the
        expected set, how far it consumed, and the captures observed before the failure.
      </li>
      <li>
        The share button gzips the selected grammar id and input into the URL hash, so a link
        reproduces the playground state without an account or storage.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Grammar source is shown read-only in this release: compiling PARG text in the browser
      needs the compiler as a wasm module, which is tracked as the next playground milestone.
      The shipped artifact is the contract the runtime consumes.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
